  - DeepSeek’s R1 release triggered the largest single-day loss in Nvidia's history because it demonstrated that a frontier-class, open-weights reasoning model could be trained for a fraction of the incumbent cost [Source: ev-1].
  - This development challenged the market thesis that AI capital expenditure and Nvidia demand were protected by compute scale, leading to a repricing of this belief on January 27, 2025 (represented as 1/27/2025 or 2025-01-27) when Nvidia lost approximately US$589 billion in market capitalization [Source: ev-1].
  - At that time, about US$1 trillion was erased across the tech complex [Source: ev-1].
